        "id": "vsf-1-lesson-2",
        "title": "Unit 1 · Systems and Records",
        "kind": "reading",
        "body": "## Use the System That Answers the Question\n\nA good dispatcher knows where to look and what a record can tell them. Switching between screens is useful only when you are checking the same vehicle and the same event.\n\n**Towbook and TowCentric** support dispatch, billing and vehicle records. **Auto Data Direct** supports ownership and lienholder information checks. A record in one system may help explain another, but it should not be treated as interchangeable with every other document.\n\n## Build a Reliable Vehicle Record\n\nStart with the identifiers. Confirm the plate or VIN and relevant vehicle details before you rely on a note, photograph or payment entry.\n\nThen connect the information the next person will need:\n\n1. **The event:** Which tow or storage record is this?\n2. **The people and roles:** What has been verified about ownership or other interests?\n3. **The activity:** What has been reported, completed or approved?\n4. **The evidence:** Where are the condition photographs and supporting documents?\n5. **The open item:** What remains unresolved and who is handling it?\n\nRelease photographs show the vehicle’s condition when it leaves storage. Keep them with the correct record so another shift can find them. A useful note identifies the issue and the next step without asking a coworker to reconstruct your whole conversation.\n\n## Explain a Fee Without Guessing\n\nA **notification fee** relates to notifying the owner or lienholder about storage. Knowing that purpose is different from knowing that a particular amount is allowed in a particular case.\n\nCheck the current approved fee schedule, notice timing and applicable conditions before quoting or collecting a charge. A remembered training example does not authorize a live fee.\n\nYou can keep the customer informed while checking: “I’m reviewing the applicable charges and notice record so I can explain the total accurately.” Give the verified explanation once the record is clear.\n\n## Prepare the Next Shift\n\n:::practice What Would You Do?\n**Hypothetical:** You find a vehicle’s ownership information in Auto Data Direct and a release photo saved under a similar vehicle in Towbook. The next shift begins in ten minutes. What would you verify and hand off?\n\nPause and put your response into your own words before opening the coaching.\n:::coach\nCheck the identifiers before relying on or moving any record. Use the approved correction process for a mismatch. Tell the next shift which vehicle you verified, what is wrong, what action is underway and what remains open. Do not silently treat a similar record as the right one.\n:::\n\n## Reference Material\n\n:::reference Complete original lesson and source references\n### Systems and Records\n\n- **Towbook / TowCentric** manage dispatch, billing and stored-vehicle records.\n- **Auto Data Direct** supports ownership and **lienholder** information checks.\n- **Release photographs** document vehicle condition when the vehicle leaves storage.\n\n### Fees and Current Policy\n\nA **notification fee** relates to notifying the owner or **lienholder**; the allowed amount, notice timing, and conditions must be checked against the **current approved policy**. Do not treat a legacy training example as permission to charge a fee. The source exam and complete study guide are available to instructors for review.\n\n**Source:** Vehicle Storage Facility Glossary Study Guide #1\n:::",
