        "kind": "reading",
        "body": "## Put the First Unit to Work\n\nYou now have the vocabulary and record tools needed to begin a useful conversation. The next skill is using them together while someone is waiting for help.\n\nPicture a caller who knows their car was towed but does not know the tow type or which document to bring. Your job is to turn that uncertainty into a clear next step.\n\n## Work Through a Simple Call\n\n1. **Listen to the request.** Find out whether the person needs to locate a vehicle, understand the record or arrange the next step.\n2. **Identify the correct vehicle.** Use the identifiers required by the current process.\n3. **Understand the event.** Distinguish a PPI, consent tow or incident-management situation using the record.\n4. **Check the relevant roles.** Do not assume that driver, registrant, owner and lienholder all mean the same person.\n5. **Use the appropriate system.** Review the operational record and any ownership or lienholder information needed for the task.\n6. **Explain the next verified action.** Be clear about what the customer can do and what still needs review.\n\nYou do not need to use every industry term in every conversation. You do need to understand the terms well enough to avoid sending the customer down the wrong path.\n\n## Check Understanding Before Ending the Call\n\nA helpful closing brings the conversation back to the person: **“Before we finish, let’s make sure the next step is clear.”**\n\nSummarize what you confirmed, the action the customer can take and any unresolved item. If a fee or document question needs checking, say so rather than giving a confident guess.\n\nThe knowledge check asks you to recognize these terms and their purposes. Review any distinction you cannot yet explain in plain words. This course records internal company learning; it does not issue a state license or approved continuing-education credit.\n\n## Explain It in Your Own Words\n\n:::practice What Would You Do?\n**Hypothetical:** A new coworker says, “Towbook tells us who the lienholder is, so whoever is named there can automatically pick up the car.” How would you help them slow down and check the reasoning?\n\nPause and put your response into your own words before opening the coaching.\n:::coach\nSeparate the system’s record from the release decision. Towbook supports the operational record; ownership and lienholder checks may involve Auto Data Direct and supporting documents. A recorded role does not replace the current release procedure. Ask which vehicle, which role and which authority have actually been verified.\n:::\n\n## Reference Material\n\n:::reference Complete original lesson and source references\n### Before the Knowledge Check\n\nReview the terms and systems before starting the knowledge check. These questions were selected from VSF Exam Unit 1 and checked against its study guide. The full legacy exam is preserved separately for instructor review because its answer key is explicitly marked “Outdated.”\n\n### Internal Training\n\nThis is internal company training. It is not a state-issued license, state examination, or approved continuing-education credit.\n\n**Source:** Vehicle Storage Facility Glossary Study Guide #1\n:::",
