        "id": "vsf-2-lesson-3",
        "title": "Unit 2 · Make the Release Handoff Clear",
        "kind": "reading",
        "body": "## Walk Through a Release Handoff\n\nYou have checked documents, reviewed the vehicle record and explained the customer’s next step. Now imagine another employee taking over. Could they tell what is complete and what still needs attention?\n\nThis unit brings the pieces together: **cab card details, parking addenda, vehicle records, charges, courtesy-release approval and release photographs**. The goal is an accurate handoff that another person can use.\n\n## Use Four Questions to Check Your Work\n\n1. **Do the identifiers match?** A cab card has a unit number, VIN and permit type. The vehicle record and photos must also belong to the correct vehicle.\n2. **Am I using the right rule?** A property parking addendum addresses property parking terms. A release procedure addresses the release task. Use each for its actual purpose.\n3. **Is the money decision verified?** Distinguish a charge from an authorized no-charge exception. Keep the approval and reason visible in the record.\n4. **Does the evidence reflect release time?** Confirm the release-photo timing and that the images are stored with the vehicle in Towbook.\n\nIf one answer is unclear, describe that gap. A specific unresolved item can be reviewed. A general “everything looks fine” note gives the next employee little to work with.\n\n## Make the Customer’s Next Step Understandable\n\nUse a short explanation that connects the remaining task to its purpose. For example: **“I’m checking the approval note so I can confirm the correct release arrangement.”**\n\nDo not fill a silence with an old fee, remembered legal deadline or unsupported promise. The current approved process controls those details. The knowledge check focuses on the stable document, record and evidence concepts you have practiced here.\n\nComplete Unit 1 before this unit’s check. A passing result lets you continue through the Dispatch VSF learning path.\n\n## Practice a Useful Shift Note\n\n:::practice What Would You Do?\n**Hypothetical:** A colleague leaves a note that says, “Customer is coming. Paperwork okay. Ask about fees.” Rewrite the handoff as a list of facts you would need to verify.\n\nPause and put your response into your own words before opening the coaching.\n:::coach\nIdentify the vehicle, which documents were checked, any mismatch, which charges were verified, whether a courtesy-release request is pending, and the release-photo status. Mark unknown items as unknown. Do not invent details to make the note look complete.\n:::\n\n## Reference Material\n\n:::reference Complete original lesson and source references\n### Topics in This Knowledge Check\n\nThis knowledge check uses the stable records, documents and evidence topics in VSF Exam Unit 2. The full source exam includes pricing, jurisdiction and legal questions and a visible cab-card answer-key conflict. That source exam remains in instructor review until corrected.\n\n### Your Learning Path\n\nComplete Unit 1 first. Passing this knowledge check unlocks the next course in the Dispatch VSF pathway.\n\n**Source:** Vehicle Storage Facility Glossary Study Guide #2\n:::",
